# inv-patch: 25-l6-desc
# purpose: L6 oracle, Mode D descriptor size (spec I4 L6, H8): IAU_INV_DESC_BYTES=32|40|64 sets the SQ descriptor size on both sides (nvmf_tgt reads it once at transport create in iau_inv_desc_init(); the host library reads it at load time; same strtoll rule, any other value = the LOCKED 40 B). Layouts in 64-bit words: 40 B = LOCKED {w0 opc/fuse/cid/nlb-1/control, w1 slba, w2 cookie (tr), w3 cb_arg, w4 cb_fn}, 1.6 per 64 B line; 32 B = {w0, w1, cb_arg, cb_fn} (only the cookie w2 is dropped: the target never reads it, the host finds the tracker by cid, so every field the target decodes and this workload uses survives), 2 per line; 64 B = the 40 B descriptor at a 64 B stride, words 5..7 never written or read, 1 per line. Target: iau_fetch_one() keeps the original 40 B code (instruction-identical at -O2 plus one load+compare+not-taken branch) and tail-calls an out-of-line 32/64 B fetch; the descriptor-ring map length is qsize x the size. Host (20's inv_flags architecture): the descriptor ring is allocated at num_entries x the size; 32, exactly 40 and 64 set INV_F_DESC (0x40) on Mode D IO qpairs (not Mode E: 32/64 there fail construct with -ENOTSUP, 40 sets no bit), the stock submit's single inv_flags test now covers INV_F_SUBMIT = TRFREE|DESC and tail-calls inv_submit_lever(), which runs 20's trfree submit (now always inlined into it) or inv_desc_submit (a copy of the stock Mode D tracker submit that writes the sized descriptor through inv_write_desc; a request that is not a read or write of at most 128 KiB fails with -ENOTSUP, logged once); 20's trfree submit and 22's I-thin write use inv_write_desc only when INV_F_DESC is set (otherwise their original stores, so 22 and 20 arms with the env unset are unchanged apart from one inv_flags test in the I-thin write). INV_F_DESC without a rec bit completes through 23's lever record loop with 4 words (the rec32 shape), so INV_F_DESC at exactly 40 is the L6 control: read desc32/desc64 against desc40 (the descriptor-size effect) and desc40 against unset (the lever dispatch cost). The levers compose with 20 (trfree), 22 (I-thin) and 23 (record size). With the env unset no bit is set, nvme_pcie_qpair_submit_request compiles to the same instructions as before except the immediate of its one inv_flags test (and the call target), and stock nvme_pcie_qpair offsets are unchanged (inv_desc_b and inv_desc_logged at the tail)
# safety: SAFE for this workload (perf reads and writes of at most 128 KiB, the cookie is never read by the target); the descriptor format != the LOCKED RTL/gem5 format (overlay only, never in spdk/)
# breaks: descriptor format != LOCKED RTL format (overlay only); 32 B drops the cookie w2 (host tracker pointer; the target ignores it and the host finds the tracker by cid), 64 B only pads; nvmf_tgt and the host must see the same IAU_INV_DESC_BYTES (run_point exports it to both): a disagreement misparses every descriptor and usually hangs perf (no timeout; it can also crash on a garbage callback), and check_l.py FAILs the point when the target's INV_DESC line is missing, carries another env value, or gives other bytes than the host's construct lines; Mode D only (mode 0 ignores it); a host qpair with Mode E and a size other than 40 fails construct with -ENOTSUP; an IO qpair with the env at 32, 40 or 64 fails requests that are not reads or writes of at most 128 KiB with -ENOTSUP (no stock fallback); per-IO cycle records are not taken on the lever paths (non-lean builds only); oracle overhead the design would not pay: one inv_flags test in 22's thin write, a size branch per descriptor write, the inv_submit_lever dispatch and one load+compare per target fetch. §4 L evidence (printed only when IAU_INV_DESC_BYTES is non-empty, the target's rule): host "INV_DESC qid=N bytes=B per_line=K" per Mode D IO qpair at construct and, at destroy, "INV_DESC qid=N all K cids returned at destroy (bytes=B)" only when that qpair's cid pool is whole (the same rule as 23: thin stack, else trfree stack, else every tracker on free_tr and outstanding_tr empty), else an ERROR line with "lost IO"; target "INV_DESC target: env=V bytes=B per_line=K" at transport create (per_line = 64/B in integer division, so 1 for 40 B); check_l.py expects one destroy line per qpair in mode 4 and the size agreement above
# env: IAU_INV_DESC_BYTES=32|40|64, read by BOTH nvmf_tgt and the host (target default 40 = the LOCKED fetch; the host sets INV_F_DESC only when the env is set and non-empty, never from the default; exactly 40 = the desc40 lever-path control, unset = the stock paths)
